9 {\cf20 // High Level Goals}\par
10 {\cf20 //}\par
11 {\cf20 // - Serve as the runtime/DDI representation for all D3D11 tokenized code,}\par
12 {\cf20 //   for all classes of programs, including pixel program, vertex program,}\par
13 {\cf20 //   geometry program, etc.}\par
14 {\cf20 //}\par
15 {\cf20 // - Any information that HLSL needs to give to drivers is encoded in}\par
16 {\cf20 //   this token format in some form.}\par
17 {\cf20 //}\par
18 {\cf20 // - Enable common tools and source code for managing all tokenizable}\par
19 {\cf20 //   program formats.}\par
20 {\cf20 //}\par
21 {\cf20 // - Support extensible token definitions, allowing full customizations for}\par
22 {\cf20 //   specific program classes, while maintaining general conventions for all}\par
23 {\cf20 //   program models.}\par
24 {\cf20 //}\par
25 {\cf20 // - Binary backwards compatible with D3D10.  Any token name that was originally}\par
26 {\cf20 //   defined with "D3D10" in it is unchanged; D3D11 only adds new tokens.}\par
27 {\cf20 //}\par
28 {\cf20 // ----------------------------------------------------------------------------}\par
29 {\cf20 //}\par
30 {\cf20 // Low Level Feature Summary}\par
31 {\cf20 //}\par
32 {\cf20 // - DWORD based tokens always, for simplicity}\par
33 {\cf20 // - Opcode token is generally a single DWORD, though there is a bit indicating}\par
34 {\cf20 //   if extended information (extra DWORD(s)) are present}\par
35 {\cf20 // - Operand tokens are a completely self contained, extensible format,}\par
36 {\cf20 //   with scalar and 4-vector data types as first class citizens, but}\par
37 {\cf20 //   allowance for extension to n-component vectors.}\par
38 {\cf20 // - Initial operand token identifies register type, register file}\par
39 {\cf20 //   structure/dimensionality and mode of indexing for each dimension,}\par
40 {\cf20 //   and choice of component selection mechanism (i.e. mask vs. swizzle etc).}\par
41 {\cf20 // - Optional additional extended operand tokens can defined things like}\par
42 {\cf20 //   modifiers (which are not needed by default).}\par
43 {\cf20 // - Operand's immediate index value(s), if needed, appear as subsequent DWORD}\par
44 {\cf20 //   values, and if relative addressing is specified, an additional completely}\par
45 {\cf20 //   self contained operand definition appears nested in the token sequence.}\par
46 {\cf20 //}\par
47 {\cf20 // ----------------------------------------------------------------------------}\par
